\* GENERATED BY THE GAP-DETECTION HARNESS - do not edit by hand.
\*
\* Fires when an input is pending that no action of Next can consume: an event
\* arrived in a state the spec text defines no handling for. Stays silent when
\* the protocol simply ends, because the implication is vacuous once nothing is
\* pending - which is what plain deadlock checking got wrong.
EXTENDS core_4_19_4_3

InputAlphabet == {"BLE_Connect", "DPLE_Update", "GATT_Exchange_MTU", "GATT_Discover", "Initiate_BTP_Session", "Receive_Handshake_Request", "Receive_GATT_Write_Response", "Receive_C2_Subscription", "Receive_Handshake_Response", "BTP_Conn_Rsp_Timeout_Client", "BTP_Conn_Rsp_Timeout_Server"}

NoUnhandledInput ==
    (pendingInput # NoInput)
        => ENABLED (Next /\ pendingInput' # pendingInput)

NoUnhandledInputOperational ==
